.TH AINIX 1 "November 2026" "AINIX 0.11" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ainix \- local NixOS assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ainix
[\,OPTIONS\/] [\,QUERY\/]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AINIX answers NixOS questions from the files on this machine.
A newcomer gets plain words and the next edit.
An advanced user who names an option gets the file, the current line, and one official page.
.PP
A question is docs-first:
.IP 1 3
Built-in notes for packages, rebuilds, flakes, generations, and Home Manager.
.IP 2 3
Nix on this computer.
A dotted option is passed to
.BR nixos-option .
Other questions go to
.BR "nix search nixpkgs" .
Results are cached under
.IR ~/.local/share/ainix/ .
.IP 3 3
DuckDuckGo HTML search, with
.I nixos
added to the query, only if Nix found nothing and the machine is online.
.IP 4 3
Ollama, only if the three steps above miss.
The prompt includes this machine's layout, a short package-file excerpt when the question is about packages, the file hits, and any text already found.
The model is told not to invent options or paths.
.PP
AINIX then reads
.I /etc/nixos ,
or the directory in
.BR AINIX_NIXOS_CONFIG .
A
.I flake.nix
in the current directory is ignored.
.PP
A how-to prints plain words, the file to edit, and the rebuild command, then the matching line and one
.I search.nixos.org
link.
A question that names an option, or asks for a default or a type, leads with the line and that link.
The search page is printed and is not downloaded.
.PP
.B ainix install
and
.B ainix rebuild
do not search the web.
They read the local config and print a preview.
.B install
names the file that assigns
.IR environment.systemPackages .
.B rebuild
prints
.I sudo nixos-rebuild switch
on a channels system, or
.I sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake <dir>#<name>
on a flake.
.PP
.B ainix home
shows a Home Manager switch command if a config is detected.
.PP
Nothing is edited.
Nothing runs unless you pass
.BR \-\-execute .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B help
Show this usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Recent queries.
.TP
.B \-\-note TEXT
Save a note.
.TP
.B \-\-cache-clear
Clear the Nix doc cache.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the curl-installed files.
.TP
.B \-\-model NAME
Ollama model to use.
Optional.
.TP
.B \-\-model-first
Ask the local model before the docs.
.TP
.B \-\-docs-first
Docs, Nix, and the web before the model.
This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-execute, \-x
Run a control command.
Asks unless
.B \-\-yes
is set.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Skip the confirm prompt on execute.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AINIX_NIXOS_CONFIG
Directory that holds the NixOS config.
The default is
.IR /etc/nixos .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ainix/config.json
Optional settings, for example
.IR '{"model": "gemma2:9b", "model_first": true}' .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/
History, notes, and the doc cache.
.SH NOTES
The model is optional.
Ollama is the local model and makes no NVIDIA or AMD assumption.
AINIX does not edit config files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix (1),
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR nixos-option (8)
